<title>USA: Morrison Knudsen gets $200 million clean-up.</title>
<headline>Morrison Knudsen gets $200 million clean-up.</headline>
<dateline>BOISE, Idaho 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morrison Knudsen Corp said it will perform engineering and construction services totaling more than $200 million for the largest privatization effort ever undertaken at the Idaho National Engineering Laboratory (INEL) by the Department of Energy (DOE).</p>
<p>Morrison Knudsen said it was working as part of a team led by BNFL Inc. The total life cycle cost of the project will total $1.189 billion.</p>
<p>BNFL Inc. is the U.S. subsidiary of BNFL, an international nuclear fuel-cycle and radioactive waste management services company headquartered in the United Kingdom.</p>
